{
  "summary": "Random weight checks for athletes are organised and are the responsibility of the IJF Education and Coaching Commission, and are carried out for individual events only with no random weigh-in for IJF Mixed Team events [SOR-2026-08-P079-S096]. For IJF World Judo Tour events the random weigh-in opens one hour before the start of the competition each day, and the time limit to arrive is 30 minutes or 6 contests before the athlete’s first contest at the latest [SOR-2026-08-P079-S096]. Athletes must bring their accreditation for identification, and their weight cannot be more than 5 percent higher than the official maximum weight limit of the category [SOR-2026-08-P079-S096].",
  "normative_basis": "Sport and Organisation Rules of the International Judo Federation, Section 6.3 Random Weigh-in [SOR-2026-08-P079-S096] and WEIGH-IN [SOR-2026-08-P074-S085].",
